# source: SYNTHETIC
# title: Ring limit: nobody answers, 480 near the limit, slot freed, next INVITE rings
# verdict: DIFFERS
# basis: sip_dialog_test.py phases 4-5; real limit 45 s, here 1 s
# ring-ms: 1000
# reason: cosmetic, Portico is the correct one: gate-sip's 480 carries a NEW To tag (it clears the call before replying, so reply() mints one), Portico reuses the call's own tag as RFC 3261 requires for a final response. The real station probably never sees it: it gives up ringing on its own at about 27 s, before the 45 s limit

>>> send
INVITE sip:9901@{{SRV}} SIP/2.0
Via: SIP/2.0/UDP {{ST}};branch=z9hG4bKinv1
From: <sip:8001@{{ST}}>;tag=st-call-1
To: <sip:9901@{{SRV}}>
Call-ID: call-1
CSeq: 1 INVITE
Contact: <sip:8001@{{ST}}>
Content-Type: application/sdp
Max-Forwards: 70

v=0
o=- 0 0 IN IP4 {{STIP}}
s=-
c=IN IP4 {{STIP}}
t=0 0
m=audio {{RTP}} RTP/AVP 97 8 0 18 9 102 103 101
a=rtpmap:97 PCM/16000
a=rtpmap:8 PCMA/8000
a=rtpmap:0 PCMU/8000
a=rtpmap:18 G729/8000
a=rtpmap:9 G722/8000
a=rtpmap:102 G722/16000
a=rtpmap:103 PCM/8000
a=rtpmap:101 telephone-event/8000
m=video 20000 RTP/AVP 96
a=rtpmap:96 H264/90000
.
>>> recv
>>> recv window=1500ms
>>> state
>>> send
INVITE sip:9901@{{SRV}} SIP/2.0
Via: SIP/2.0/UDP {{ST}};branch=z9hG4bKinv5
From: <sip:8001@{{ST}}>;tag=st-call-5
To: <sip:9901@{{SRV}}>
Call-ID: call-5
CSeq: 1 INVITE
Contact: <sip:8001@{{ST}}>
Content-Type: application/sdp
Max-Forwards: 70

v=0
o=- 0 0 IN IP4 {{STIP}}
s=-
c=IN IP4 {{STIP}}
t=0 0
m=audio {{RTP}} RTP/AVP 97 8 0 18 9 102 103 101
a=rtpmap:97 PCM/16000
a=rtpmap:8 PCMA/8000
a=rtpmap:0 PCMU/8000
a=rtpmap:18 G729/8000
a=rtpmap:9 G722/8000
a=rtpmap:102 G722/16000
a=rtpmap:103 PCM/8000
a=rtpmap:101 telephone-event/8000
m=video 20000 RTP/AVP 96
a=rtpmap:96 H264/90000
.
